export anchor CassetteJCardStyle:
    number: 93
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Cassette J-card
    idea: The dashboard is a home-made mixtape, with the week written on a cassette label, the projects as a hand-lettered track list on a folded J-card with tape counters and reels, and the chart as segmented recording levels.
    base: light
    palette:
        desk: #eceef0, the page
        card: #fbfaf6, the J-card, labels and panels
        shell: #d9dce1, the cassette shell and the header
        shellLine: #9aa0aa, shell edges and fold lines, never text
        print: #222428, printed text and counters
        grey: #575c66, small print and day letters
        penBlue: #1f3a8a, handwriting, this week segments and focus
        ruledLine: #c9d3e6, label lines, never text
        labelRed: #c8323a, label stripes and the focus ring
        recordRed: #ad2530, the primary button, track numbers, overdue and Behind
        mint: #9fd8c8, a cover stripe, never text
        lilac: #c7b8e6, a cover stripe, never text
        peach: #f6c39b, a cover stripe, never text
        tape: #5a4a3a, tape wound on the reels
        green: #23663f, On track
        amber: #8a5100, At risk
    type:
        Three stacks. Handwriting uses Marker Felt, Segoe Print, Bradley
        Hand, Chalkboard SE, Comic Sans MS, cursive in pen blue for the
        52px greeting, 40px label numbers, 22px track names, times, the
        user and the search. Printed text uses Eurostile, Microgramma, Bank
        Gothic, Michroma, Verdana at 15px, with 11 to 15px bold caps
        tracked 0.2em for labels and 34px caps on the cover. Counters and
        track numbers use SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas at 700 and 15 to 18px.
    layout:
        A grey deck strip holds the brand handwritten on a white tape
        label with a red top stripe, nav as raised keys with a 3px bottom
        edge where the current key is black and pressed down, a search
        with handwritten placeholder, a red key with a record dot for New
        project, a bell key and the user in pen. The top row has Side A
        Home, a tilted handwritten Good morning, Mara, the date in caps and
        a red boxed line with a record dot saying 4 tasks are overdue.
        Beside it a cassette shell carries a label with a red, peach and
        lilac stripe, the title this week's mix and the four numbers
        handwritten over caps labels, above a tape window with two reels.
        The J-card unfolds as a front cover with diagonal pastel stripes
        and Projects mix vol. 6, a vertical spine with a red stripe, and a
        wide flap with the track list. Each track has a red mono number,
        the handwritten name, team, tasks and due date, a black three digit
        tape counter showing the percentage, two reels whose tape has
        wound from left to right by the percentage, and the status. Below,
        a recording log and a levels chart where each day is a column of
        segments, one segment per task. Below 960px the J-card panels
        stack and the spine turns horizontal.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 10px per track row and 32px between the cassette, the card and panels.
    density: Medium. Each track packs a name, a counter, reels and a status into one row.
    corners: 14px on the cassette shell, 6px on the label, 3px on keys and fields, square on the J-card.
    borders: 1px shell grey on paper, dashed fold lines between card panels and 3px bottom edges on keys like a tape deck.
    shadows: One soft drop under the J-card. Keys press down by losing their thick bottom edge.
    icons:
        Tape deck transport marks with the caps word. On track is Play, At
        risk is Pause, Behind is Rewind and overdue is the round Record
        dot.
    focus: A 2px pen blue outline offset 2px, then a card coloured gap and a 2px label red ring.
    tone: A friend's mixtape, such as this week's mix, Track list, Recording log and Rec 4 tasks are overdue.
